PHZ100-071400-

302 PM HST Wed Aug 6 2025



.Synopsis for Hawaiian coastal waters...

 Winds will be light east or variable today as a weak low

associated with the remnants of former Tropical Cyclone Gil

passes north of the islands. Moderate to locally fresh trades

will return Thursday through Friday as high pressure far

northeast of the state briefly takes control. Depending on the

track of Tropical Storm Henriette, light trades may again be

disrupted this weekend. 



