Generalized Statewide Coastal Waters Forecast for Hawaii

National Weather Service Honolulu HI

304 PM HST Wed Aug 6 2025



.Synopsis for Hawaiian coastal waters...

 Winds will be light east or variable today as a weak low

associated with the remnants of former Tropical Cyclone Gil

passes north of the islands. Moderate to locally fresh trades

will return Thursday through Friday as high pressure far

northeast of the state briefly takes control. Depending on the

track of Tropical Storm Henriette, light trades may again be

disrupted this weekend. 



$$



Hawaiian waters within 40 nautical miles including the channels-



...SMALL CRAFT ADVISORY FROM THURSDAY MORNING THROUGH EARLY FRIDAY

MORNING FOR MAALAEA BAY...THE PAILOLO AND ALENUIHAHA CHANNELS AND

WATERS SOUTH OF THE BIG ISLAND...



.TONIGHT...East winds 15 to 20 knots. Seas 4 to 6 feet. Wave

Detail: East 4 feet at 9 seconds and south southwest 3 feet at

20 seconds. Scattered showers. 

.THURSDAY...East winds 20 to 25 knots. Seas 5 to 7 feet. Wave

Detail: East 5 feet at 7 seconds and south southwest 3 feet at

20 seconds. Scattered showers. 

.THURSDAY NIGHT...East winds 20 to 25 knots. Seas 6 to 9 feet.

Wave Detail: East 5 feet at 7 seconds and south southwest 5 feet

at 18 seconds. Isolated showers. 

.FRIDAY...East winds 20 to 25 knots. Seas 6 to 9 feet. Wave

