Hazardous Weather Outlook

National Weather Service Wichita KS

806 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



KSZ032-033-047>053-067>072-082-083-091>096-098>100-080115-

Russell-Lincoln-Barton-Ellsworth-Saline-Rice-McPherson-Marion-Chase-

Reno-Harvey-Butler-Greenwood-Woodson-Allen-Kingman-Sedgwick-Harper-

Sumner-Cowley-Elk-Wilson-Neosho-Chautauqua-Montgomery-Labette-

806 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



This hazardous weather outlook is for portions of Central Kansas,

South Central Kansas and Southeast Kansas.



.DAY ONE...Tonight



Storm chances will be possible across the Flint Hills around

sunrise. Strong to severe storms are not expected.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Thursday through Tuesday



Afternoon heat indices above 100 degrees are expected to continue

through Saturday with the highest values expected on Friday.



Storm chances will return for Saturday night through Tuesday 

morning as a cold front moves into the area. A few strong storms 

will be possible with this activity. 



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...



Spotter activation is not anticipated tonight.



